## Architecture

```
canopy/
├── canopy/
│   ├── core/
│   │   ├── renderer.py      # Main rendering engine
│   │   ├── seeded_random.py # Deterministic RNG
│   │   └── grid.py          # Grid manipulation
│   ├── effects/
│   │   ├── effects.py       # Effect pipeline
│   │   └── presets.py       # Sacred presets
│   ├── archive/
│   │   └── database.py      # Archive storage
│   └── __init__.py
├── server.py                # FastAPI endpoints
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

---

## The Archive Philosophy

> You do not need to save heavy, bloated video files to remember what the canopy looked like yesterday. You only need to save the holy seed, the timestamp, and the manipulation variables.

The Archive embodies this philosophy. Instead of storing megabytes of pixel data, we store the *mathematical seeds* that generate those pixels. With the same seed, we can always regenerate the exact same visual state.

---

## WebSocket Protocol

Connect to `/ws/live` for real-time streaming:

```javascript
// Set a new seed
ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "set_seed", seed: 42 }));

// Set effect parameter
ws.send(JSON.stringify({
    type: "set_param",
    effect: "bloom",
    param: "intensity",
    value: 0.5
}));

// Request a frame render
ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: "render" }));

// Apply grid deformation
ws.send(JSON.stringify({
    type: "grid_deform",
    params: { type: "wave", params: { amplitude: 0.05, frequency: 10 } }
}));
```

